From: kanata-nicola
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:08:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] tcp server: take ChangeLayer and the requests only

The TCP server has no authentication: any process on the machine can connect,
including those of other users and sandboxed applications that share the host
network. Besides switching the layer, it could make kanata load a
configuration file of its choice (ReloadFile, and Reload*), act on virtual keys
(ActOnFakeKey) or move the mouse (SetMouse). A configuration that kanata loads
this way decides what every key does, and can also report keys to the
connected clients.

kanata-nicola uses the port for IME sync, which sends ChangeLayer only. Take
ChangeLayer and the requests that change nothing (Hello, Request*); answer any
other command with an error and disconnect the client, as for an invalid
message.
---
--- a/src/tcp_server.rs
+++ b/src/tcp_server.rs
@@ -190,6 +190,30 @@
                                 match v {
                                     Ok(event) => {
                                         log::debug!("tcp server received command: {:?}", event);
+                                        // Only ChangeLayer and the requests that change nothing. Any local
+                                        // process can connect (there is no authentication), and the other
+                                        // commands would let it load another configuration, act on virtual
+                                        // keys or move the mouse.
+                                        if !matches!(
+                                            event,
+                                            ClientMessage::ChangeLayer { .. }
+                                                | ClientMessage::RequestLayerNames {}
+                                                | ClientMessage::RequestFakeKeyNames {}
+                                                | ClientMessage::RequestCurrentLayerInfo {}
+                                                | ClientMessage::RequestCurrentLayerName {}
+                                                | ClientMessage::Hello {}
+                                        ) {
+                                            log::warn!(
+                                                "client sent a command that this build does not take, disconnecting them: {event:?}"
+                                            );
+                                            let response = ServerResponse::Error {
+                                                msg: "command not taken: this build takes ChangeLayer and requests only"
+                                                    .to_string(),
+                                            };
+                                            let _ = stream.write_all(&response.as_bytes());
+                                            connections.lock().remove(&addr);
+                                            break;
+                                        }
                                         match event {
                                             ClientMessage::ChangeLayer { new } => {
                                                 kanata.lock().change_layer(new);
